      "translatedText": "- `std::array<T, N>`Encapsulates a fixed\\-size array whose size is determined at compile time\\.\n- Has the standard interface of STL containers (`size()` , `at()` , iterators, etc\\.)\\.\n- Can be assigned as a whole, and does not decay to a pointer when passed to a function, so size information is not lost\\.\n- Suitable for scenarios where the size is known at compile time, and is more lightweight than `vector`\\.",
